      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":826,
          "quote": "Only\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\nare not ordered among themselves.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":819
        }
      ],
      "key": "result_recording_and_standing",
      "statement": "Every performed evaluation returns exactly one core value directly or by refinement and records its predicate and original domain outcome. Consumers needing domain distinctions must read that outcome, whose definer retains its meaning. Result standing concerns what the predicate establishes and is distinct from commitment standing: only satisfied establishes it; falsified establishes failure and names its counterexample; the other three establish neither and identify deciding evidence, missing declaration with owner where supplied, or basis repair. Satisfied stands above each other value in predicate support; those four have no universal mutual order. No refinement or mapping raises standing; failure or undecidability cannot become success, and unknown effect completion cannot become no effect or completed.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["core_result_algebra", "result_conjunction", "construction_result_predicates"],
      "conditions": [
        "An evaluation was required or planned but was not performed."
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":847,
          "quote": "Not performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":840
        }
      ],
      "key": "nonperformance_has_no_result",
      "statement": "There is no closed result and an actor cannot report having performed the evaluation. Non-performance maps neither to indeterminate nor any other core value. A missing result enters each relevant conjunction as a missing planned assessment if planned, otherwise uncovered required coverage. Failed, indeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope and invalid-basis outcomes follow their declared algebra without coercion to satisfied.",
