      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":869,
          "quote": "The refinement names the question it\nanswers and the predicate its mapping is for, and maps every refined value\nto exactly one core value. No outcome exists outside the core; a\nrefinement adds no core value and keeps the pressure of `indeterminate`,\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` explicit. Where a refined value would\nmap to one of two core values according to its cause, the cause is part of\nthe refined value and each resulting value maps once",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":863
        }
      ],
      "key": "refinement_total_mapping_and_parent_rule",
      "statement": "Name the question, mapping predicate and values; map every refined value to exactly one core value without adding a core value or hiding indeterminate, out_of_frame or invalid_basis pressure. Cause-dependent core mappings must encode the cause in separate refined values. Each child names parent and cause and retains its parent's core value; changing the core requires a different parent declared only by that parent's owner. Each definer states its mapping where it defines its values; ACTIVATION §3 owns admission, activation and step refinements. A further split cannot alter what the parent establishes.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
