      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":919,
          "quote": "Where the\nclaim also depends on an undeclared relation or capability,\n`out_of_frame` and `indeterminate` each have a lawful ground; the result\nnames the value it returns and that ground, and this boundary excludes\nneither (P5).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":915
        },
        {
          "end_line":939,
          "quote": "In either case\nthe unexercised part, B above, has no result: in every conjunction over\nit, it is a planned assessment without a closed result, and the known\nfailure A survives with it ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)).\nThe evaluation's result and the step's stop state answer different\nquestions, so the step's stop value never becomes the evaluation's\nresult.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#FOUNDATIONS%2F4.%20Algebra%2FResults",
          "start_line":933
        }
      ],
      "key": "frame_evidence_and_unexercised_capability_boundary",
      "statement": "Out_of_frame is grounded in an activated frame's missing material relation or capability, regardless of exercise; it names what is missing, its owner where given and reconfiguration pressure. A required undefined term is an undeclared material relation because its meaning can alter the result without a declared input. Indeterminate is grounded in insufficient admissible evidence and names what evidence would decide. Leaving a declared required capability unexercised creates no special value: return whatever sufficient evaluation or applicable judgment supports, including falsified from a counterexample to A in A-and-B, which agreement cannot discard. Otherwise the evaluation is unperformed, the step's construction-availability stop is incomplete, and work state retains the unexercised capability as a residual. The unexercised part remains a missing planned assessment in either case. Stop state cannot substitute for evaluation result.",
